# Frontend (SvelteKit)

## API & types

- All HTTP via `$lib/api` (`api`, `apiEnvelope`). No raw `fetch` in routes.
- Types in `$lib/types`; mirror backend envelope and `snake_case` JSON fields.

## State

- **`let`:** local UI only (open/closed, draft input).
- **Stores:** cross-route/session data (`activeCampaignStore`, etc.). Do not keep shared API data only in one component.

## UI copy (players/GMs, not engineers)

- Errors: "Failed to load Campaign" — never stack traces or HTTP jargon.
- Buttons: **Create** (not Add/New), **Delete** (not Remove), **Save** (not Update).
- Paired stats: `Current / Max` (e.g. `25 / 30`).

## Theming

- Base: paper white bg, dark ink text.
- **Player** accent: red (`--accent-player` / `--accent-primary` on player layouts).
- **GM** accent: gold (`--accent-gm` / `--accent-primary` on GM layouts).
- Set accents in role `+layout.svelte`; **never** hardcode accent hex in leaf components.

## Reuse

Extend `BaseModal`, tables, etc. with props/slots — do not copy markup.

## Role dashboard sub-pages

Routes **one segment** below a role dashboard are sub-pages. Role dashboards themselves never show a back control.

| Role | Dashboard route | Dashboard `title` (parent name) | Sub-page pattern |
|------|-----------------|----------------------------------|------------------|
| GM | `/gm` | `Game Master Dashboard` | `/gm/<slug>` |
| Player | `/player` | `Player Dashboard` | `/player/<slug>` |

Sub-pages use `DashboardPage` and **must** wire `BackButton` in `headerActions` before `LogoutButton`:

- `href`: parent dashboard route (`/gm` or `/player`) — use `goto`, never `history.back()`
- `parentTitle`: exact `title` string from the parent dashboard page

Example (`/gm/system-management`):

```svelte
{#snippet headerActions()}
	<BackButton href="/gm" parentTitle="Game Master Dashboard" />
	<LogoutButton />
{/snippet}
```

Do not add `BackButton` on `/gm`, `/player`, or the landing page (`/`).
